! Silicon with a PAW dataset, for an augmented ultracell calculation. The k-grid is
! 4 2 2 so that a four-cell ultracell at kgrid = (1, 2, 2) folds onto exactly it.
!
! ecutrho is set to 4 ecutwfc explicitly, which a PAW dataset does not ask for
! (8 to 12 is its own dual, and that runs too since PLAN.md P88 stage 9). It is
! kept here because every committed comparison against a real supercell is at
! this pair on both sides, and because at 4 the supercell's dense FFT box is
! exactly the tiled one, where at a dual it is not -- see OPEN.md Part X item 3.
!
! Symmetry is off because a modulation breaks the crystal's point group, and
! the grid is unshifted because the folded set k0 + Q is a Monkhorst-Pack grid
! only if its origin is.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 10.20,
    nat = 2, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 16.0, ecutrho = 64.0,
    nosym = .true., noinv = .true.
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-12
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pz-n-kjpaw_psl.0.1.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS automatic
 4 2 2 0 0 0
